[{"text":"EpsContractFreeQ[exp] returns True if the expression contains epsilon tensors that can be contracted with each other. The function is optimized for large expressions, i.e. it is not so good as a criterion in e.g. Select.","anchor":"epscontractfreeq"},{"text":"Overview, Contract, EpsContract.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"FCI[LC[p1, p2, p3, p4]] EpsContractFreeQ[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{p1}\\;\\text{p2}\\;\\text{p3}\\;\\text{p4}}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{True}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCI[LC[p1, p2, p3, mu] LC[q1, q2, q3, q4]] EpsContractFreeQ[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{p1}\\;\\text{p2}\\;\\text{p3}\\;\\text{mu}} \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{q1}\\;\\text{q2}\\;\\text{q3}\\;\\text{q4}}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{False}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"}]